/T (Most ignored instinct.  Devendra Sinha understood both.  Without looking away from us, he continued.  "The difference is that I learned something you haven't." "What?" I asked.  "The truth isn't enough."  I didn't understand what he meant at the time.  Years later, I would.  He opened another file and looked directly at us.  "Officially, this investigation is now yours."  For a moment, I felt relief.  Then he continued.  "You have one week."  The relief vanished immediately.  "One week?" Vikram repeated.  "Seven days," ACP Sinha replied. "Find evidence. Find a witness. Find anything I can place in front of people who only believe what they can stamp, sign, and archive." )
